Copied from github.com/superfly/flyctl, package wg, at commit 3b3a0588b
(Apache-2.0, see LICENSE in this directory).

wg6pn changes, each marked "wg6pn addition" in the source:
- package renamed to flywg; flyctl-internal logger/terminal imports removed
  (WG6PN_WG_DEBUG=1 enables verbose WireGuard logs)
- Config.PeerAddr: the provisioned peer IP is added as a second netstack
  address, so inbound connections to it are accepted
- Tunnel.ListenTCP, Tunnel.Addrs, and a rebuild channel closed on reprovision
- removed a stray debug print in the resolver
- PersistentKeepAlive (25s) and the peer address on both token-mode and
  API-registered tunnels (legacyTunnelConfig): the websocket plugboard drops
  inbound frames until the device has sent once
- removed a stray debug print in doConnect
- inbound_test.go: real WireGuard inbound path, and device-speaks-first
- TestListenTCPAcrossReprovision in ws_token_test.go

wg6pn connects with ConnectWS only. The token-mode code (ConnectToken,
token.go and its websocket handling) is kept from upstream but unused.
